>> title: Baba Ganoush
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: eggplant, tahini, middle eastern, dip, grill
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, Deli
>> aka: baba ghanoush, babaghanouj, baba ghannouj, moutabal, mutabbal, eggplant dip
>> pairs-with: pita-bread, muhammara
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.1: char 15 min until collapsed
>> step.2: drain 20 min
>> step.3: mash to a paste
>> step.4: whisk in
>> step.5: fold in, mash coarse
>> step.6: season

Char @eggplants{2%lb}(900 g; 2 medium) directly over a #gas flame{} for ~{15%min}, turning, until the skins blister black and the flesh collapses.

Drain the scooped flesh of @&(~1)charred eggplant{} in a #sieve{} for ~{20%min}, discarding the bitter liquid.

Mash @garlic{2%cloves} with @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} and @lemon juice{2%Tbs}(30 mL) to a paste.

Whisk @tahini{1/3%cup}(80 g; well stirred) into @&(~1)garlic paste{}.

Fold @&(~3)drained eggplant{} into @&(~1)tahini{}, mashing with a fork to keep it coarse.

Season @&(~1)baba ganoush{} with @ground cumin{1/4%tsp}, @flat-leaf parsley{2%Tbs}(chopped), and @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}.
